WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.512
Hannah: Total cost of ownership includes engineering. The monthly bill isn't the whole comparison.

2
00:00:07.512 --> 00:00:14.256
Raj: Vertical scaling adds eighteen hundred monthly. That's fleet cost, not just primary.

3
00:00:14.256 --> 00:00:20.809
Anika: Shards add roughly twenty-four hundred monthly. Engineering could take eight weeks or longer.

4
00:00:20.809 --> 00:00:28.009
Priya: Just to confirm, estimates, not quotes, right? And no guaranteed sharding savings yet.

5
00:00:28.009 --> 00:00:35.737
Lukas: Correct, migration risk increases testing effort. On-call ownership adds ongoing staffing costs.

6
00:00:35.737 --> 00:00:43.153
Raj: Storage expansion adds four hundred monthly separately. Both options still need that capacity.

7
00:00:43.153 --> 00:00:51.409
Hannah: Query optimization needs about two engineer-weeks. Savings stay provisional until load tests.

8
00:00:51.409 --> 00:00:57.626
Priya: Okay, what's the ETA for firm quotes? We have bandwidth for one pilot.

9
00:00:57.626 --> 00:01:05.114
Lukas: Tomorrow for infrastructure estimates and lead times. Maybe procurement changes the delivery assumptions.

10
00:01:05.114 --> 00:01:11.930
Anika: So, favor queries plus storage preparation. Keep the larger instance as contingency.

